          "id": "issue-01",
          "factId": "f6",
          "severity": "minor",
          "verdict": "imprecise",
          "claim": "研究提示，持续查看前任动态与更强的思念、更慢的恢复相关；这不是意志力问题，而是每次查看都在重新激活同一套奖赏回路。",
          "problem": "持续查看前任动态与思念、恢复较差的相关性有研究支持，但“每次查看都在重新激活同一套奖赏回路”是推测机制：原研究测量的是自我报告与恢复指标，并未同步扫描奖赏回路，因果表述过强。",
          "correction": "社交媒体延长了分手的可见性。研究提示，持续查看前任动态与更强的思念、更慢的恢复相关；这更像反复被触发的渴求，而不是单纯的意志力问题。",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "title": "Facebook surveillance of former romantic partners: associations with postbreakup recovery and personal growth",
              "url": "https://doi.org/10.1089/cyber.2012.0125",
              "quote": "Facebook surveillance was associated with greater breakup-related distress, more negative feelings, greater longing for the former partner, and lower levels of personal growth."
            },
            {
              "title": "REF 2021 impact case study: recovery from relationship breakdown",
              "url": "https://results2021.ref.ac.uk/impact/6c361fc3-99c5-4ae3-a048-2b15e5ca58ec/pdf",
              "quote": "Facebook surveillance was associated with greater breakup-related distress, more negative feelings, greater longing for the former partner, and lower levels of personal growth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "issue-02",
          "factId": "f7",
          "severity": "minor",
          "verdict": "unsupported",
          "claim": "研究观察到，社交圈重叠越多，分手后接触越难避免，恢复也越容易被拖慢；这不是要求朋友选边，而是需要重新划定信息边界。",
          "problem": "没有可靠研究直接检验“社交圈重叠越多、接触越难避免、恢复越慢”这条完整链条；现有综述指出，分手后接触与恢复的关系是条件性的，取决于对分离的接受、共同义务、动机与接触形式，不能一概而论。",
          "correction": null,
          "evidence": [
            {
              "title": "Romantic Relationship Dissolution and the Possibility of Post-Breakup Friendship: A Narrative Review",
              "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/22178937",
              "quote": "Evidence concerning contact is conditional: acceptance of the separation, shared obligations, motives, and the form of contact matter."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "sourceNotes": [
        "Marshall (2012) 与 Slotter & Ward (2015) 均为相关性或日记研究，不能单独支撑强因果表述。"
      ],
      "summary": "神经影像与追踪研究支撑分手痛、奖赏渴求与自我概念变化的总体叙述；社媒查看的机制表述与社交圈重叠推论两处已降级。"
